// comb.js — combinatorics: factorial, nCr, nPr, Pascal, Bell, Stirling.
//
// Provenance: 2026-07-22 (Alfred completion sweep, applied-math lane).
// Reference chapter 15-comb.slat documents 13 verbs; none were wired. This
// file wires all 13 with honest combinatorics.
//
// Doctrine:
//   * Every verb is a pure function on integers. Non-integer inputs are
//     truncated silently (matches the flexible-input convention in
//     lib/math/basic.js for gcd/lcm).
//   * Bell / partition-count / Catalan use recurrences with a small memo
//     table so B(20) etc. stay fast without global state.
//   * Numeric range: results overflow JS `number` (2^53) once n gets big
//     (~n=170 for factorial). We don't switch to BigInt here — the
//     reference documents this as a caveat ("safe range n<25 for Bell").

